virtual-clock: read the time from the harness's virtual clock

Classification: harness plumbing.

_plat__RealTime() returns difftest_virtual_ms(), the harness's virtual clock
in milliseconds (testing/src/bin/shared/ffi.rs,
testing/src/differential/server.rs). It starts at the reference process's
CLOCK_MONOTONIC milliseconds and advances only when the harness advances it,
so the TPM's Clock and Time follow tpm-rs's virtual clock exactly. The
original implementation is kept, renamed and unused, to keep the patch
small. difftest_virtual_ms is the only symbol the patched reference imports
from the harness.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/Platform/src/Clock.c b/TPMCmd/Platform/src/Clock.c
--- a/TPMCmd/Platform/src/Clock.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/Platform/src/Clock.c
@@ -68,7 +68,18 @@ clock_t debugTime;
 //*** _plat__RealTime()
 // This is another, probably futile, attempt to define a portable function
 // that will return a 64-bit clock value that has mSec resolution.
+// tpm-rs differential testing: the real time is the harness's virtual clock
+// (see testing/src/differential/server.rs), which starts at the reference
+// process's CLOCK_MONOTONIC milliseconds and advances only when the harness
+// advances it. The original implementation is kept below, unused.
+extern uint64_t difftest_virtual_ms(void);
+
 LIB_EXPORT uint64_t _plat__RealTime(void)
+{
+    return difftest_virtual_ms();
+}
+
+static uint64_t _plat__RealTime_unused(void)
 {
     clock64_t time;
 #ifdef _MSC_VER
